    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99">

                <pb facs="0230" n="164" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v02/pg164"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">762.9411/21: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Toyko</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-27T22:00:00+09:00">September 27, 1940—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 27—2:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>909. At 9:45 o’clock tonight we were given by the Foreign Office the following
                    four documents in English translation shortly before their release to the press: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Summary of the three-power pact between Japan, Germany and Italy
                            signed on September 27, 1940 at Berlin;</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Radio address by the Minister for Foreign Affairs;</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Imperial rescript by the Emperor;</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>Message of the Prime Minister.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>In view of the prime importance of these documents in connection with the present
                    critical crisis and being informed that complete texts may not be cabled to the
                    American press, I feel obliged to telegraph documents numbers 2, 3, and 4 in
                    full so that Department may study their tone and substance without delay. The
                    texts follow <pb facs="0231" n="165" xml:id="pg165"/> in three ensuing
                    telegrams. The summary of the pact<anchor n="6" xml:id="d99-f1"/> itself had
                    already been announced on the radio from the United States tonight.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d99-f1" n="6" xml:id="d99-f1-content">
                <p>Summary of pact as transmitted to the Department by the Ambassador in Japan in
                    his despatch No. 5038, October 5, 1940, is printed <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
